From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Barrios <25010449+nbarrios@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:02:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] crfpmoc: Use a persistent seed and a stable user id

FP_SEED is write-once per FPMCU boot and, together with the FP_CONTEXT
user id, keys the encryption of every template. Upstream picks both at
random on every open, so stored prints stop matching after fprintd
restarts or a reboot.

Read the 32-byte seed from /var/lib/fprint/crfpmoc-seed (created once with
getrandom(2), directory 0700, file 0600) and refuse it if it is not a
regular root-owned file with no permission bits outside 0600, or if its
directory is not root-owned or is group/world writable. Derive the user id
as SHA-256("crfpmoc-userid-v1" || seed).

Only set the seed if FP_ENC_STATUS does not report FP_ENC_STATUS_SEED_SET,
and treat EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED from FP_SEED as 'already set' instead of a
failure. Emulation mode keeps the fixed test seed and context.

Trade-off: the seed is stored in plaintext rather than sealed to the TPM;
see crfpmoc-seed.h.
